  "rationale": "With memoryDump:credentialAccess blocked, the AND steps that need it fail: ssoLogin:authenticate and dbLogin:authenticate. That cuts off appServer:lateralMovement (via ssoLogin) and backupHost:lateralMovement (via dbLogin). Losing those also cuts off secretsManager:privilegeEscalation (needs backupHost and ssoLogin), domainAdmin:privilegeEscalation (needs dbLogin and the blocked jumpHost) and serviceAccount:privilegeEscalation (needs the blocked jumpHost). Every parent of the target then fails: vaultRead needs backupHost; codeRepo needs backupHost, secretsManager or jumpHost; dbReplica needs appServer or domainAdmin; mailArchive needs secretsManager, jumpHost or serviceAccount. So crownData:exfiltrate is unreachable."
